-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can you short-term rental in Little River?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Generally yes, under unincorporated Horry County rules plus any HOA restrictions, but Little River is more of a primary-residence, second-home, and Intracoastal-boating market than a high-volume nightly-rental market. Verify county zoning and HOA documents by address.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Little River good for boating and fishing?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A working Intracoastal Waterway waterfront: seafood restaurants on the docks, marinas, offshore fishing, Calabash cruises, casino boats, and the annual Blue Crab Festival, all near the North Carolina line.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Little River cheaper than the oceanfront towns?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Generally yes. Median prices have run in the high $200,000s to low $300,000s in early 2026, below the oceanfront markets, which is a big part of its appeal.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are property taxes on a second home in Little River?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In Little River that makes a second home's bill about 3.3 times a primary home's on the same house.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which schools serve Little River?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Public schools fall within Horry County Schools, with high-school students generally attending North Myrtle Beach High School. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment on the district boundary map.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Little River more affordable than the central beaches?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Pricing tends to be more approachable than the central Grand Strand, and the area has been a steady growth corridor.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is Little River known for?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A fishing and boating identity at the northern end of the Grand Strand near the North Carolina line.</p></div></div></section>
