+</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River sits on the Intracoastal Waterway, the boat channel behind the Grand Strand's beaches. At the end of Mineola Avenue, the old village meets the water, with docks, boats and waterfront restaurants. Coquina Harbour, a marina, is about 3 minutes away by car.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-waterfront-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-waterfront-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-waterfront-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="1131" alt="The Intracoastal Waterway at Little River from above: a slip basin full of boats ringed by condo buildings, labelled Mariner's Pointe, and docks with boats at the end of a street, labelled Waterfront" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The waterfront at the end of Mineola Avenue, and the slip basin at Mariner's Pointe, from above.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A bridge built in 1935 still swings open for boats. The swing bridge on Sea Mountain Highway turns its 217-foot span on a center pier. SCDOT counts it among the oldest swing-span highway bridges in its inventory, and it is eligible for the National Register.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It opens for boats on signal. On weekdays that are not federal holidays, from 7 to 9 a.m. and 4 to 6 p.m., it opens only on the hour and half hour.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens, a county park on the waterway, has about 3 miles of trails and boardwalks through more than 115 acres of forest and marsh. A piece of the original Kings Highway, the colonial road from Boston to Charleston, still runs at the front of the park, behind the CB Berry Community Center.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach at Cherry Grove Pier in North Myrtle Beach, Calabash in North Carolina and McLeod Seacoast hospital are all within about 11 minutes by car, as the map shows. The airport is the long drive, about 41 minutes.</p><figure class="c3-lr-fig" style="max-width:560px"><div class="c3-lr-frame"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-little-river" viewBox="0 0 360 288" width="360" height="288" role="img" aria-label="Map of Little River and the coast: from the old village, the beach at Cherry Grove Pier is about 11 minutes 