width="128.7" height="36" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-little-river-shopping" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="11.9" y="-24.9"><tspan x="11.9">Barefoot Landing</tspan></text><text class="m" x="11.9" y="-9.4">about 18 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(230.5 100.5)"><g class="k"><g transform="scale(0.8)"><ellipse cx="0" cy="1" rx="7" ry="2.4" fill="#1c2028" opacity=".18"/><path d="M0 0C-3-6-13-14-13-26a13 13 0 1 1 26 0c0 12-10 20-13 26z" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5"/><use href="#c3r-little-river-home" x="-8.5" y="-34.5" width="17" height="17" color="#ffffff"/></g><text class="h" x="-15" y="-14.5" text-anchor="end"><tspan x="-15">Little River</tspan></text></g></g></g></svg></div><figcaption>Drive times by car from the old village, without traffic. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River is a place people live all year. When the Census last counted, about one in five of its homes was kept for seasonal use. In North Myrtle Beach, next door, it was nearly half.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Share of homes kept for seasonal use, 2020 Census"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Share of homes kept for seasonal use, 2020 Census</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Place</span><span role="columnheader">Seasonal homes</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.968" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">48%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Garden City</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.79" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">39%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.382" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">19%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All of Horry County</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.352" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">18%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.272" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Carolina Forest</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.092" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">5%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.034" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">2%</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Homes no one lived in on Census Day that were kept for seasonal or occasional use, such as vacation homes and many nightly rentals.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="town-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Town or county">Is Little River, SC a town?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Little River has no town government and no town limits, so Horry County makes its rules and collects its tax. The Census Bureau counts it as a census designated place, a named community that is not incorporated.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">With no town, a home you live in pays no city tax. It pays about $368 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value, plus an $89.40 county fee.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One corner is different. A small part of the Little River ZIP code along the waterway is inside the city of North Myrtle Beach. Its homes, about 250 and mostly condos, have a Little River address and pay North Myrtle Beach's city tax. We check which side of the line a house is on.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="on-the-water"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="On the water">Living on the water in Little River: boat slips, ramps and waterfront homes</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River is where Horry County's deeded boat slips are. About two of every three slips in the county that are sold as real estate, with their own deed and tax bill, are here, at three marinas.</p><figure class="c3-lr-fig"><div class="c3-lr-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-water-map.svg" width="760" height="495" alt="Map of Little River on the water. The Intracoastal Waterway runs along its south edge, and the Waccamaw River along its north-west edge. Three marinas with deeded boat slips sit on the waterway near the old village: 1 Mariner's Pointe, the largest, east of the village, and 2 Coquina Harbour and 3 Lightkeepers Village side by side to the south-west. The public landings, marked A, are on the waterway at the US 17 bridge. FEMA's high-risk flood zone, striped blue, lies along the water. North Myrtle Beach is shaded south of the waterway." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><ul class="c3-lr-key" aria-label="Map key"><li><span class="c3-lr-num marina" data-n="1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Mariner's Pointe</span></li><li><span class="c3-lr-num marina" data-n="2" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Coquina Harbour</span></li><li><span class="c3-lr-num marina" data-n="3" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Lightkeepers Village</span></li><li><span class="c3-lr-num sq" data-n="A" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>T. Craig Campbell Landing and, across the waterway, Johnny Causey Landing</span></li><li><span class="c3-lr-sw" style="background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#3d7fb8 0 3px,#b9d3e6 3px 7px)"></span><span>FEMA's high-risk flood zone</span></li><li><span class="c3-lr-sw" style="background:#e3d9cc"></span><span>The city of North Myrtle Beach</span></li></ul><p style="margin:.7rem 0 0">The dark line is the Little River ZIP code. Marker sizes follow the number of deeded slips. The two landings on the Waccamaw River are north-west of this map. Map data: Horry County GIS; FEMA flood map as the county carries it; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.</p></figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most marinas rent their slips. A deeded slip is one you buy and own, and the county sends it a tax bill like a house. The county values most of the deeded slips here at $35,000 to $45,000.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:49.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Deeded boat slips and what they sold for, from county deeds</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Marina</th><th scope="col" class="n">Deeded slips</th><th scope="col" class="n">Sold in the past year</th><th scope="col">Prices</th><th scope="col">Middle price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Mariner's Pointe</th><td class="n" data-label="Deeded slips">116</td><td class="n" data-label="Sold in the past year">11</td><td data-label="Prices">$10,000 to $38,000</td><td data-label="Middle price">$16,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Coquina Harbour</th><td class="n" data-label="Deeded slips">81</td><td class="n" data-label="Sold in the past year">0</td><td data-label="Prices">No sales</td><td data-label="Middle price">No sales</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Lightkeepers Village</th><td class="n" data-label="Deeded slips">25</td><td class="n" data-label="Sold in the past year">1</td><td data-label="Prices">$95,000</td><td data-label="Middle price">One sale</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Dock Holidays Marina, in North Myrtle Beach</th><td class="n" data-label="Deeded slips">93</td><td class="n" data-label="Sold in the past year">10</td><td data-label="Prices">$65,000 to $115,000</td><td data-label="Middle price">About $92,500</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A slip at Mariner's Pointe has sold for far less than one across the line at Dock Holidays. The county's records do not give a slip's length or the depth of the water, and the price depends on both. We find out both for any slip you like.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where to launch a boat</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County runs two public boat landings in the Little River ZIP. T. Craig Campbell Landing is on the Intracoastal Waterway at the US 17 bridge, about 7 minutes from the old village, with two ramps, a dock and a paved lot. Johnny Causey Landing, across the waterway from it, has two ramps and a larger paved lot and is just inside North Myrtle Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Waccamaw River, Worthams Ferry Landing has one ramp and an unpaved lot. Chris Anderson Landing, on the river near Longs, has two ramps.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Homes on the water</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few houses here sit on the water. About 1.5 percent of the houses in the ZIP have a lot on the Intracoastal Waterway, a canal off it, or the Waccamaw River.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most homes within about 50 feet of the water are condos. About half of all the homes by the water are in three condo communities: Carolina Yacht Landing, Mariner's Pointe and Lightkeepers Village.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo by the water usually sold for about $263,000 in the past year, and one away from it for about $180,000. Houses on the water are rare: only 5 resold, and the middle one sold for about $1.3 million.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A resold house at about $357,000 and a Mariner's Pointe slip at about $16,500 come to about $375,000 together. If you would rather keep the boat on a trailer at home, our <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to homes with no HOA</a> covers where that is allowed.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="parts"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Five parts">Which part of Little River should you look at?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River's homes fall into five parts, and each has something the others do not. The numbers on the map match the entries below. Prices are what homes resold for in the past year, from county deeds.</p><figure class="c3-lr-fig"><div class="c3-lr-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-parts-map.svg" width="760" height="483" alt="Map of Little River's subdivisions as dots, coloured by part and numbered: 1 the old village and the harbors, on the waterway; 2 north and east, toward the North Carolina line; 3 north-west, toward the Waccamaw River; 4 west, around the hospital; 5 far west, at SC 9, where the Carolina Bays Parkway ends." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption>Each dot is a subdivision, sized by its homes. Map data: Horry County GIS; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.<ol class="c3-lr-key" aria-label="The five parts of Little River"><li><span class="c3-lr-num p-village" data-n="1" aria-hidden="true"></span><a href="#old-village">The old village and the harbors</a></li><li><span class="c3-lr-num p-east" data-n="2" aria-hidden="true"></span><a href="#north-and-east">North and east, toward Calabash</a></li><li><span class="c3-lr-num p-northwest" data-n="3" aria-hidden="true"></span><a href="#north-west">North-west, toward the Waccamaw</a></li><li><span class="c3-lr-num p-west" data-n="4" aria-hidden="true"></span><a href="#west">West, around the hospital</a></li><li><span class="c3-lr-num p-farwest" data-n="5" aria-hidden="true"></span><a href="#far-west">Far west, at SC 9</a></li></ol></figcaption></figure><h3 id="old-village" data-toc="The old village and the harbors" class="c3-lr-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-lr-num p-village" data-n="1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>The old village and the harbors: the boats at your door</span></h3><div style="margin:.4rem 0 1.1rem"><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><strong>Marinas</strong><span class="t">All three</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Homes</strong><span class="t">Condos and houses</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>Flood risk</strong><span class="t">By the water</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This is the part to choose if the boat comes first. The waterfront at the end of Mineola Avenue and all three marinas with deeded slips are here, within about a mile of the village center. At Mariner's Pointe, the condo buildings ring the slip basin.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-harbours-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-harbours-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-little-river/little-river-harbours-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="1217" alt="A marina basin full of boats off the Intracoastal Waterway, from above, with Coquina Harbour labelled at its upper end, Lightkeepers Village near its mouth and US 17 across the top" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Coquina Harbour and Lightkeepers Village share one basin off the waterway, just south of US 17.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cypress Village is the largest subdivision, with houses and townhouses, and its homes resold for about $385,000. Hidden Lakes Village is a neighborhood of houses at about $318,000. Condos at Gardens at Cypress Bay resold for about $150,000, among the lowest prices in Little River.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The trade-off is flood risk by the water. About half the condos at Mariner's Pointe are in FEMA's high-risk zone, and most of the homes at Eastport.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Little%20River's%20old%20village">Get the homes for sale in Little River's old village<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="north-and-east" data-toc="North and east, toward Calabash" class="c3-lr-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-lr-num p-east" data-n="2" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>North and east, toward Calabash: Heather Glen and Vereen Gardens</span></h3><div style="margin:.4rem 0 1.1rem"><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Largest</strong><span class="t">Heather Glen</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5.5 21c.5-3 7.5-2.5 7.5-6.5S7.5 10.5 8 6.5M17.5 9.3V13"/><circle cx="17.5" cy="6.5" r="2.8"/><circle cx="8.2" cy="4" r="1.2"/></svg></span><span><strong>County park</strong><span class="t">Vereen Gardens</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Nearest</strong><span class="t">Calabash, N.C.</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Heather Glen is Little River's largest subdivision, with more than 1,100 houses, north-east of the old village. It also had the most resales in the past year, at a middle price of about $375,000. Heather Lakes, east of it, sold at the same middle price.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This is the side nearest Calabash, North Carolina. Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens is in this part too, between US 17 and the waterway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Windjammer Village mixes houses with a few manufactured homes and resold for about $310,000. Its trade-off is the water: 15 of its homes are in the high-risk flood zone.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=east%20Little%20River">Get the homes for sale in east Little River<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="north-west" data-toc="North-west, toward the Waccamaw" class="c3-lr-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-lr-num p-northwest" data-n="3" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>North-west, toward the Waccamaw: dry ground and a river ramp</span></h3><div style="margin:.4rem 0 1.1rem"><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>Flood zone</strong><span class="t">Outside it</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><strong>River ramp</strong><span class="t">Worthams Ferry</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 16v-4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h10.5l2 5M14.5 11l4-7H21M8.5 17.5h4M2 21.5h20"/><circle cx="6.5" cy="17.5" r="2"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="17.5" r="2"/></svg></span><span><strong>Lafayette Park</strong><span class="t">Quarter-acre lots</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every home in this part's subdivisions is outside FEMA's high-risk zone. Worthams Ferry Landing, the county's ramp on the Waccamaw River, is just north of this part.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Lafayette Park has more than 400 houses on lots of about a quarter of an acre, at a middle resale price of about $348,000. River Hills, closer to the old village, resold for about $385,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Farther out, North Village resold for about $313,000. Stones Edge mixes houses and manufactured homes and had few resales; the middle one sold for about $230,000. The trade-off is the distance to the waterway and the marinas.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=north-west%20Little%20River">Get the homes for sale in north-west Little River<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west" data-toc="West, around the hospital" class="c3-lr-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-lr-num p-west" data-n="4" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>West, around the hospital: the highest prices, and condos on the water</span></h3><div style="margin:.4rem 0 1.1rem"><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 3h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2zM12 7.5v9M7.5 12h9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Hospital</strong><span class="t">In this part</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Prices</strong><span class="t">The highest</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><strong>Condos</strong><span class="t">On the water</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">McLeod Seacoast hospital is in this part. Among Little River subdivisions with at least five resales, the two highest prices are here: Sawgrass Village at Bridgewater, about $585,000, and Waterside Village, about $560,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carolina Yacht Landing, on the waterway west of Campbell Landing, is a condo community, and about half its units are within about 50 feet of the water. They resold for about $252,000. Bay Tree, near the hospital, has condos and townhouses at about $165,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Pointe has the most manufactured homes of any subdivision in the ZIP, and the few that resold had a middle price of about $180,000. The trade-off here is the distance to the old village and its marinas, about 2 to 3 miles.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=west%20Little%20River">Get the homes for sale in west Little River<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="far-west" data-toc="Far west, at SC 9" class="c3-lr-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-lr-num p-farwest" data-n="5" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Far west, at SC 9: where the parkway begins</span></h3><div style="margin:.4rem 0 1.1rem"><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>The parkway</strong><span class="t">Starts here</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Waterfall</strong><span class="t">Among the highest</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>Flood zone</strong><span class="t">Outside it</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Carolina Bays Parkway, SC 31, begins at SC 9 at the edge of this part, and its planned extension north would start there too. Hidden Brooke, a neighborhood of houses about a third of a mile from that junction, resold for about $390,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Waterfall had few resales, at a middle price of about $555,000, among the highest in Little River. Palm Lakes Plantation resold for about $340,000. All of their homes are outside FEMA's high-risk zone.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The trade-off is distance. This is the farthest part from the old village and its marinas.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=far%20west%20Little%20River">Get the homes for sale in far west Little River<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="What homes resold for in subdivisions with 10 or more resales, past year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What homes resold for in subdivisions with 10 or more resales, past year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Subdivision, part of Little River</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Waterside Village</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 4</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$560,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Hidden Brooke</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 5</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.696" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$390,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Cypress Village, houses and townhouses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 1</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.688" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$385,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">River Hills</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 3</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.688" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$385,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Heather Glen</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 2</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.67" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$375,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Lafayette Park</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 3</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.621" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$348,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Palm Lakes Plantation</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 5</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.607" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$340,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Windjammer Village</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 2</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.554" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$310,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Carolina Yacht Landing, condos</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 4</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.45" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$252,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Bay Tree, condos and townhouses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">part 4</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.295" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$165,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Every resale in each subdivision, mostly houses unless the name says otherwise.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Little River flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of it does not. About 96 in 100 Little River homes are outside FEMA's high-risk flood zone. Homes by the water are far more likely to be inside it.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Share of Little River homes inside FEMA's high-risk flood zone"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Share of Little River homes inside FEMA's high-risk flood zone</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Homes</span><span role="columnheader">In the zone</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Homes within about 50 feet of the water</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.9" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">45%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All homes in the ZIP</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.072" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">3.6%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Homes away from the water</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.044" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">2.2%</span></span></div></div></div></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hurricanes do reach this line. Hurricane Hazel came ashore near Little River, at the North Carolina and South Carolina line, in October 1954 as a Category 4 hurricane. It hit at the year's highest tide, and the storm surge reached as high as 18 feet at Calabash.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few houses for sale at our last count were in the high-risk zone. We check the flood map, the elevation and the seller's flood disclosure for every house before you make an offer. Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how to find out if a house flooded</a> shows every record we use.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do you need flood insurance in Little River?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Federal law makes a lender require flood insurance only when the building is in FEMA's high-risk zone. A lender can still ask for it anywhere.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the Little River ZIP, a flood policy on a house outside the zone usually costs about $480 a year, and inside it about $1,250. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a> explains the other policies a house here can need.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A new federal flood policy takes effect 30 days after the application and payment are complete. It can start sooner when it is bought with a home loan, or within a year after a FEMA map change puts the building in the high-risk zone.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Little River each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a $357,000 house you live in, the property tax is about $1,400 a year. With a flood policy outside the high-risk zone, the two come to about $1,900.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Each year, for a $357,000 house outside North Myrtle Beach</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What you pay</th><th scope="col">Your home</th><th scope="col">A second home or rental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Property tax</th><td data-label="Your home">About $1,400</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $4,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Flood policy outside the high-risk zone, if you want one</th><td data-label="Your home">About $480</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $480</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tax and flood policy together</th><td data-label="Your home">About $1,900</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $4,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina taxes a home you live in on 4 percent of its value, and a second home or rental on 6 percent. The owner must apply for the lower rate. These figures take the county's value as the price and include the county fee. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax page</a> shows how to apply.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homeowners insurance is a third bill, and its price depends on the house, its roof and the company. Where there is an HOA, its fee comes on top, and we read its budget and rules with you.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="home-prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes cost in Little River, SC?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A resold house in Little River usually sold for about $357,000 in the past year. Half sold for between about $304,000 and $451,000. New houses from builders sold for less in the middle.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a home in Little River sold for in the past year, by kind"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a home in Little River sold for in the past year, by kind</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Kind of home</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">House, resold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$357,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">New house from a builder</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.89" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$318,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Townhouse</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.741" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$265,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condo</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.53" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$189,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Manufactured home on its own lot</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.511" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$183,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Sales recorded in the county's deeds for homes in the Little River ZIP code. Middle price: half sold for more, half for less.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What kind of homes are here</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About two in three homes the county taxes as real estate in the ZIP are houses, and more than a quarter are condos. About one in twenty is a manufactured home. Homes on rented lots are taxed apart and are not in that count.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Census survey, which also counts homes on rented lots, puts mobile homes at about six in every hundred homes in Little River's Census area. In Garden City it is about a third.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Room to spread out is uncommon. Fewer than one in twenty houses sits on an acre or more, and the typical house lot is about a fifth of an acre.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Homes for sale now</h3><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes for sale with a Little River address, at our last count"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes for sale with a Little River address, at our last count</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Kind, for sale</span><span role="columnheader">Middle asking price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 190 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$398,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Townhouses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 29 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.602" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$240,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Manufactured homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 19 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.627" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$250,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 180 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.482" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$192,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Lots</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about 49 for sale</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.414" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$165,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Asking prices, not sales. Listing counts from the Coastal Carolinas Association of REALTORS MLS, in aggregate.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 44 of the houses for sale were new construction, and 22 asked under $300,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="renting-out"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting out">What do homes rent for in Little River?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HUD's Small Area Fair Market Rent for a three-bedroom in the Little River ZIP is $2,100 a month, with utilities. That is above North Myrtle Beach's ZIP and Myrtle Beach's, and close to Carolina Forest's.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="HUD's fair market rent for a three-bedroom, by ZIP code"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">HUD's fair market rent for a three-bedroom, by ZIP code</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">ZIP code</span><span role="columnheader">A month, with utilities</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Longs, 29568</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,270</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Carolina Forest, 29579</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.982" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,230</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River, 29566</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.925" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach, 29582</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.828" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,880</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach, 29577</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.758" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,720</span></span></div></div></div></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HUD builds its figure from about the 40th percentile of rent plus utilities for standard two-bedroom rentals, then works out the other sizes with metro-wide ratios. It is a program figure, not a survey of three-bedroom rents here.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Rents people pay here run above the county's. The Census survey's middle gross rent in Little River's Census area is about $1,530 a month, against about $1,260 countywide, counting every rental, apartments included.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A worked example</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take a resold house at $357,000. At HUD's three-bedroom figure of $2,100 a month, a year comes to about $25,000, about 7 percent of the price. As a rental, the house pays about $4,400 a year in property tax, about 17 percent of that rent.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Insurance, upkeep, management and empty months come out of the rent too. Our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental analyzer</a> works them out for any address.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Short-term rentals</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River has no city ordinance, so county rules apply. A home in Little River outside North Myrtle Beach that is rented short term needs:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">a Horry County business license;</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">a county hospitality and accommodations account;</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">a South Carolina sales and accommodations tax account;</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">a yearly county personal property return for its furnishings, due April 30.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An HOA's rules can forbid short stays, and we read them first. See <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the short-term rental rules by town</a> and <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what a nightly rental earns by town</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="carolina-bays-parkway"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The new road">Is the Carolina Bays Parkway being extended through Little River?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It is planned but not built. The Carolina Bays Parkway, SC 31, would be extended from SC 9 north-east, passing north and northwest of Little River's old village. It would cross the state line to US 17 near Shallotte, North Carolina. It would be a multi-lane freeway, partly on new ground.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina's part is in SCDOT's current program, with land buying planned to start in 2026 and construction in 2028. North Carolina has not funded land buying or building for its part. The whole project is estimated at $797 million.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two states have named a preferred route. The final choice comes after they review the comments from the public hearings. If you like a house in the north-west part, we show you where it sits against the preferred route's map.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Little River?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The good points are the water, the price and a year-round town. The hard ones are the few houses on the water, flooding by the water, and the drive to the airport.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Deeded boat slips you can own, and public ramps on the waterway and the Waccamaw River.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Houses at about $357,000, no city tax, and the beach about 11 minutes away.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A year-round community, with the waterfront, the swing bridge and Vereen Gardens.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Few houses are on the water, and those cost far more. We pair a house with a deeded slip instead.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>On FEMA's map, close to half the homes by the water are in the high-risk zone. We check the map and the elevation first.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The airport is about 41 minutes away by car.</span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="little-river-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Little River, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Little River, SC a city, and what county is it in?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River is not a city. It is an unincorporated community in Horry County, South Carolina, at the North Carolina line, and the county runs it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is Little River from Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 18 minutes by car to Barefoot Landing and about 36 to Coastal Grand Mall in Myrtle Beach, without traffic. The airport is about 41 minutes away.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does Little River, SC flood?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes by the Intracoastal Waterway can. Nearly half the homes within about 50 feet of the water are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, against about four in every hundred of all homes.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax in Little River, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A home you live in pays only the county's property tax and a county fee, with no city tax on top. A second home or rental is taxed at a higher rate than a home you live in.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is a boat slip in Little River?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Deeded slips at Mariner's Pointe sold for $10,000 to $38,000 in the past year. Slips at Dock Holidays, across the line in North Myrtle Beach, sold for far more.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many people live in Little River, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 11,700 people lived in Little River at the 2020 Census, nearly a third more than in 2010.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Little River, SC safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. The FBI's Crime Data Explorer and the South Carolina Law Enforcement Division publish reported crime by police agency.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which schools serve Little River, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools assigns schools by address, in nine attendance areas, and none is named Little River. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/profile/Little_River_CDP,_South_Carolina?g=160XX00US4542010" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census profile</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/geography/about/glossary.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census glossary</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood policies</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/smallarea/index.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD rents</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4012a</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4013" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4013</a>, <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.org/sc-historic-bridges/s-20-bridge-over-intercoastal-waterway-horry-county" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOT swing bridge</a>, <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-33/chapter-I/subchapter-J/part-117/subpart-B/section-117.911" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">33 CFR 117.911</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/parks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county parks</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/gisweb/rest/services/Public/ParksRecreation/MapServer/1" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county boat landings</a>, <a href="https://www.weather.gov/ilm/HurricaneHazel1954" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS Hazel</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/monjnvh0/sales-tax-chart-short-term-rentals.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county rental filings</a>, <a href="https://www.ncdot.gov/projects/carolina-bays-parkway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCDOT project</a>, <a href="https://www.ncdot.gov/projects/carolina-bays-parkway/Documents/carolina-bays-extension-public-hearing-summary.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hearing summary</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountyschools.net/about-hcs/our-schools" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Schools</a>. Our counts from county parcels, flood maps and deeds. Listings in aggregate from CCMLS. Drives without traffic.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-wid